    "result_text": "Done. The full build passes.\n\n## What I changed\n\n`contactPreference` is a pure derivation from the stored email \u2014 exactly like the existing `locality` and `membershipLevel` derived fields \u2014 so I followed that established pattern rather than inventing a new one:\n\n1. **`mapper/ContactPreference.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny stateless helper `of(email)` returning `\"EMAIL\"`/`\"PHONE\"`, styled identically to `Locality`/`MembershipLevel`.\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` line wiring `contactPreference` to `ContactPreference.of(owner.getEmail())`.\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `contactPreference` read-only schema property so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n## Why this keeps structural impact low\n\n- The only Java *method* touched is the abstract `toOwnerDto` (a single annotation line, CC 1); the branch logic lives in the new isolated helper (`WMC_other` = 0). No existing function grew in complexity \u2014 I added a small cohesive unit instead.\n- Routing it through the mapper means the field is correct on **every** owner response (get/list/create/update) from one place, rather than being patched into each responder \u2014 so no divergence risk and no per-endpoint duplication.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite are green.",
